# Ship script (commit / push / deploy)

Never run `git commit`, `git push`, or `npm run deploy` as separate agent steps when the user asks to commit, push, and/or deploy.

Instead, run **one** command from the repo root:

```bash
./scripts/ship.sh "concise commit message"
```

## Flags

- `./scripts/ship.sh --deploy-only` — deploy only, no commit/push
- `./scripts/ship.sh --no-deploy "message"` — commit and push only

## Agent behavior

- After code changes, if the user wants shipping: run `./scripts/ship.sh` once with a good commit message.
- Do not re-run `git status`, `git diff`, and `git log` before shipping unless diagnosing a failure.
- Do not narrate each git/deploy sub-step; summarize the ship result briefly.
